{"maxId":0,"entries":{"copy|Screening":["u68"],"copy|HIV Testing":["u82"],"copy|Selection and Initiation of Antiretroviral Treatment":["u87"],"copy|General Care Considerations for the Older Adult With HIV":["u113"],"copy|Models of Geriatric HIV Care":["u127"],"copy|VZV Transmission":["u202"],"copy|Herpes Zoster Incidence and Risk Factors":["u209"],"copy|Acute Herpes Zoster":["u285"],"copy|Antiviral Therapy":["u289"],"copy|Analgesics":["u296"],"copy|Corticosteroids":["u302"],"copy|Adjuvant Agents":["u310"],"copy|Recombinant Zoster Vaccine":["u316"],"copy|Efficacy":["u320"],"copy|Safety and Reactogenicity":["u329"],"copy|Clinical Guidance":["u352"],"copy|No one is immune to HIV infection, and nearly 15% of people with HIV (PWH) in the United States and approximately 45% of persons worldwide are unaware of their diagnosis, presenting the greatest transmission risk.":["u68"],"copy|In most clinical settings, the prior two-step ELISA (antibody) and Western blot testing strategy has been replaced by a fourth-generation combination HIV-1/2 immunoassay that tests for both HIV-1 and HIV-2 antibodies and the HIV p24 antigen.":["u82"],"copy|Patients with a new HIV diagnosis should be connected to HIV care as quickly as possible.":["u87"],"copy|After antiretroviral initiation, the incidence of AIDS conditions drops dramatically, but ongoing and consistent therapy is imperative.":["u113"],"copy|Accompanying an increasing number of older adults with HIV is, unfortunately, a shortage of both HIV and geriatric medicine clinic providers.":["u127"],"copy|VZV is a double-stranded DNA herpesvirus that is transmitted from person to person via direct contact or airborne":["u202"],"copy|In general population studies from North America and Europe, the estimated incidence of herpes zoster in persons older than age 65 varies from approximately 10 to 14 cases per 1000 per year.":["u209"],"copy|The principal goal of the treatment of herpes zoster in older adults is to decrease the length of the acute attack and to reduce or eliminate pain.":["u285"],"copy|The guanosine analogs acyclovir, famciclovir, and valacyclovir are phosphorylated by viral thymidine kinase to a triphosphate form that inhibits VZV DNA polymerase and VZV replication (Table 107-1).":["u289"],"copy|Acute herpes zoster pain requires the use of standardized pain measures, scheduled analgesia, and close monitoring":["u296"],"copy|The anti-inflammatory effects of corticosteroids have been postulated to reduce herpes zoster symptoms but there remains controversy over their use.":["u302"],"copy|If moderate-to-severe herpes zoster pain is inadequately relieved by antiviral agents in combination with oral analgesic medications and/or corticosteroids, then other therapies to consider include gabapentin or pregabalin or neural blockade.":["u310"],"copy|The adjuvanted recombinant zoster vaccine (RZV; Shingrix©) is a powerful tool to prevent herpes zoster and PHN in older adults.":["u316"],"copy|The efficacy of RZV was demonstrated in over 30,000 immunocompetent community-dwelling elders in the randomized, blinded, placebo-controlled Zoster Efficacy Study in Adults 50 Years of Age or Older (ZOE-50) and Zoster Efficacy Study in Adults 70 Years of Age or Older (ZOE-70) (Figure 107-4).":["u320"],"copy|The only contraindication to RZV is a history of a severe allergic reaction to any component of the vaccine or after a previous dose of RZV.":["u329"],"copy|The Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices (ACIP) at the CDC recommends RZV for the prevention of herpes zoster and related complications in immunocompetent adults aged 50 or older including individuals who previously received zoster vaccine live (ZVL; Zostavax©).":["u352"]},"sequenceOffsets":[[23,174],[24,523],[25,-1],[42,506],[44,326],[54,463],[56,325],[76,359],[77,325],[91,358],[92,329],[96,388],[97,329],[106,295],[107,329],[110,365],[111,329],[120,296],[121,329],[125,408],[126,329],[146,293],[147,329],[155,270],[156,329],[163,387],[164,328],